        "procedure": "A suspension of Gd(OAc)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol, 88.48 mg) and H2php (0.1 mmol, 37.32 mg) in MeOH/CH2Cl2 (10 mL/10 mL) was treated with Et3N (0.5 mmol, 0.07 mL). The ensuing yellow solution was stirred for 6 h and subsequently filtered. The filtrate was left undisturbed to allow slow evaporation of the solvent. Yellow block-shaped single crystals of 1 suitable for X-ray diffraction formed after 2 days.",
